erent high schools  when he was a freshman he wanted to go  to a school that was highly ranked for  academics but later he decided to  audition for Toronto's Etobicoke School  of the Arts he was accepted but  unfortunately he ended up getting  expelled he said that he enjoyed his  time there but he's also admitted that  he simply wasn't cut out for such a  structure too academic environment  Reeves isn't the only actor in Hollywood  who didn't finish high school and like  many other creative young people he  thrived in alternative environments he  also had dyslexia which certainly didn't  help matters but he enrolled in a class  called respect for acting as well as  sketch and improv courses with second  city Toronto and he continued attending  these classes at night and honing his  craft Reeves is a man of many talents in  addition to acting in movies and theatre  he's also spent plenty of time on the  ice playing hockey in fact at one point  in his life he hoped to play  professionally while attending De La  Salle College in Toronto  he played goalie and he was quite the  formidable opponent he was so skilled at  net minding that he earned the nickname  the wall when he was younger Reeves  dreamed about representing Canada in the  Olympics one day but when he decided to  dedicate himself to acting he put that  dream on the back burner he continued to  play hockey on a recreational basis but  he chose to put acting first Reeves may  have started out as a young  jack-of-all-trades but he chose to  commit his life to becoming a master of  one and that decision has clearly paid  off one of Reeves his first professional  gigs was working as a correspondent on  the Canadian Broadcasting Corporation  Youth Program going great the show  focused on child prodigies who were able  to accomplish amazing things at a young  age do it they fired me after the first  year one year going great  Reeves also appeared in another local TV  production called hanging in a scripted  series about kids who attend a  Counseling Center in a rough part of  Toronto  he described hanging in as a godsend for  young actors in Toronto at the time who  were just trying to get a foot in the  door and make some connections in the  industry Reeves is not just skilled as  an actor he's also a gifted musician and  he was the bassist in a band called dog  star in the 90s and 2000's the band got  its start when Reeves ran into vocalist  Robert mail house in a grocery store in  1991 the two bonded over their mutual  love of hockey and eventually they  realized that they both liked jamming  out together - two more friends joined  the band and as their fan base grew they  started touring they even played some  pretty big festivals like Glastonbury in  England the band broke up after  releasing their second album because the  members were  busy with other commitments in  particular Rivas career was really  taking off with the popularity of the  Matrix films but this wasn't the end of  Rivas musicianship as he and Mail house  would go on to perform together some  more in a band called Becky maybe he can  whip out that bass in the next John wick  movie shredding on some strings could  totally be a useful tool in an  assassin's arsenal check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite stuff  are coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

